# text = Her nature was to be civil to enemies as well as to friends , and grateful to all the world for letting her remain alive said Humphrey Fairway resumed , with an unheeding air , to show that his words were no appendage to Humphrey's , but the result of independent reflection said a wide-spread woman whose stays creaked like shoes whenever she stooped or turned said Timothy Fairway , his eyes again travelling round suggested Grandfer Cantle said Susan Nunsuch , the wide woman , who preferred the original subject said Olly , the besom-maker said Humphrey chimed in Grandfer Cantle brightly said Fairway
