# text = All smiled upon Wildeve , and upon his tables and chairs likewise , from a general sense of friendliness towards the articles as well as towards their owner said Fairway , recognizing the matron's bonnet through the glass partition which divided the public apartment they had entered from the room where the women sat said Grandfer , peeping in the same direction , and discerning Thomasin , who was waiting beside her aunt in a miserable and awkward way Wildeve made no reply ; and probably feeling that the sooner he treated them the sooner they would go , he produced a stone jar , which threw a warm halo over matters at once said Grandfer Cantle , with the air of a man too well-mannered to show any hurry to taste it said Wildeve replied the guests , in the hearty tones natural when the words demanded by politeness coincide with those of deepest feeling added Grandfer Cantle said Christian said Wildeve , with condescension said Grandfer Cantle said Sam ; and the mead then circulated said Timothy Fairway , feeling demands upon his praise in some form or other he continued , to Grandfer Cantle , raising his voice so as to be heard through the partition said Christian said Sam said the furze-cutter Fairway recommenced , as one opening a new vein of the same mine of interest .
