# text = Acoustic pictures were returned from the darkened scenery ; they could hear where the tracts of heather began and ended ; where the furze was growing stalky and tall ; where it had been recently cut ; in what direction the fir-clump lay , and how near was the pit in which the hollies grew ; for these differing features had their voices no less than their shapes and colours resumed Wildeve she softly said , taking his hand As Eustacia uttered the latter words she retired from the base of the barrow , and Wildeve followed her , so that the reddleman could hear no more .
