# text = Fairway had meanwhile concluded a critical gaze at Yeobright he said to the rest of the room said Yeobright , surveying the firm figure of Fairway said Grandfer Cantle , rising and placing himself something above half a foot from Clym's eye , to induce the most searching criticism said Fairway , taking the candle and moving it over the surface of the Grandfer's countenance , the subject of his scrutiny irradiating himself with light and pleasant smiles , and giving himself jerks of juvenility said Yeobright appended Fairway decisively said the pleased ancient said Humphrey , in a low rich tone of admiration , not intended to reach anybody's ears said Grandfer Cantle said Timothy inquired Christian , drawing nearer said Timothy reproachfully said Christian said the Grandfer By this time the mummers were preparing to leave ; but Mrs .
