# text = He would ask Eustacia to agree with him in his self-condemnation ; and when she , seared inwardly by a secret she dared not tell , declared that she could not give an opinion , he would say Sometimes his condition had been one of utter remorse , unsoftened by a single tear of pure sorrow : and then he writhed as he lay , fevered far more by thought than by physical ills he said one day when in this mood said Eustacia Eustacia replied said the wretched man Eustacia was always anxious to avoid the sight of her husband in such a state as this , which had become as dreadful to her as the trial scene was to Judas Iscariot .
